    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Personal Collection",
    "overview": "White gallery space makes the objects, not the interface, the subject. Dark viewing chambers isolate reflective metal and enamel so a medal reads as a collectible physical object.\n\nOrdinary achievements use the 珐琅圆章 family: complete raised serif numerals on shallow convex enamel fields, with distinct perimeter shapes and metal finishes for each series. Rarer achievements gain layered silhouettes, intricate metalwork and richer material effects. The perfect-month piece is an eight-petal gold and pearl rosette with individually framed petals, a ridged gold inner starburst and a central crystal setting.\n\nUsage, growth and lifetime achievements also use named sculptural motifs: orbital structures, moon relief, ascending folds, radiating dawn, stepped milestones and a three-dimensional infinity loop. Each sculptural challenge uses its own motif, silhouette and internal linework. These are collection objects rather than numerical discs. When available, an earned sculptural piece leads the featured stage.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Quiet white collection space; concentrated dark object viewing.",
      "Real reflective depth and front/back exploration after unlocking.",
      "Sparse controls, fine borders and gently curved surfaces.",
      "Complexity grows with achievement difficulty."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Object Owns Color Rule",
        "body": "Keep interface surfaces neutral; numeric series identity belongs to raspberry daily, teal weekly, plum monthly and blue lifetime consistency enamel. Preserve each sculptural motif’s own material palette.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Complete Lettering Rule",
        "body": "Keep each numeral a complete independent raised form, preserving its counters and its separation from the perimeter. Use the same glyph outlines in the locked drawing.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Host Owns Navigation Rule",
        "body": "Local tabs switch collection and challenges; DSH navigation stays outside the plugin.",
        "section": "layout"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Earned Depth Rule",
        "body": "Locked objects remain line-only drawings: no material disclosure, 3D context, reverse view or rotation. Full depth and finish begin at unlock.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
